## 10. Tests and Validation

### 10.1 Validate Packs

Run:

```bash
munray validate --svc-dir <path>
```

For command help / flags:

```bash
munray help validate
```

### 10.2 Run Pack Tests

Run:

```bash
munray test --svc-dir <path>
```

For command help / flags:

```bash
munray help test
```

Test guidance:

- keep `tests/capabilities_test.lua` offline for schema discovery, validation errors, and unsupported-operation contracts
- keep `tests/integration_tests.lua` read-only and enabled by default; cover authentication, API wiring, normalization, pagination, and reads without changing remote state
- keep mutations in `tests/integraion_guarded_tests.lua`; it runs only when `MUNRAY_RUN_GUARDED=1`, uses deterministic tightly scoped fixtures, and must clean them up
- when the guarded gate is absent or not `1`, return the standard skip marker so the harness reports `SKIPPED`, not `PASS`
- `examples/*.lua` files are not executed automatically by `munray test`; add an explicit test only when you intentionally want to validate example content or behavior

